  "note": "Election of the Donaghadee Urban Council, nominations closed 4 September 1946. Only four nominations were received for the nine seats, so all four were returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 5 September 1946, p. 3). Four returned unopposed, leaving five seats unfilled. A round-up on 6 September 1946 (p. 5) instead named Mrs. Agnew, Mr. J. M'Cullough and Mr. W. Campbell as re-elected automatically and said two vacancies remained; that conflicts with the nomination list above, which is followed here. Returned unopposed."
